\section{Discussion and Conclusion}

\begin{itemize}
  \item \textbf{Privacy-NER Attention:} Achieved 99\% accuracy with minimal false positives and negatives, demonstrating strong performance on the synthetic test set.
  
  \item \textbf{Model Comparison:} Privacy-NER Attention outperformed the zero-shot baseline (62\% accuracy). Results for the DeBERTa model are pending.
  
  \item \textbf{Error Patterns:} Privacy-NER Attention had only 7 total misclassifications compared to the baseline's 113 errors.
  
  \item \textbf{Architecture Benefits:} The Privacy-NER approach leveraging named entity recognition showed clear advantages over zero-shot classification.
\end{itemize}

